  "display_title": "Freshman at Forty",
  "description": "At forty, Jeong Han-Seong finally begins the college life he’s dreamed of, enrolling as a nontraditional student after years in the corporate world. Mistaken for a professor by his much younger classmates, he struggles to find his place, until a helpful senior, Baek Cheong-Bin, steps in. With Cheong-Bin’s guidance, campus life starts to feel less overwhelming… but there’s something about the way this senior looks at him that feels anything but ordinary.\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)",
